## Selected exact built-in fields

Canonical engine-owned entry gates remain active-fixed optimizer candidates: current growth `0.25`,
annual growth `0.25`, RS `80.0`, non-M composite `70.0`, volume ratio `1.3`, and maximum buy-zone
extension `0.05`. Signal cadence is `5`. The default provider industry filter is enabled with top `20`
groups and minimum group size `3`.

The M evaluator/state machine records:

- `<50` rows: score `0.4`, bearish, no latest close.
- Follow-through search: minimum input `5`, window `30`, rally reset below `-0.01`, rally starts above
  `0.0`, and follow-through requires higher volume.
- Evaluator EMAs `[21, 50, 200]` use pandas `adjust=true`. A newly constructed stateful tracker defaults
  to `correction`; with fewer than `2` history rows bootstrap returns without changing or seeding it.
  Otherwise bootstrap uses EMA `200` with `adjust=false`: strict latest close above latest EMA selects
  `confirmed_uptrend`, otherwise `correction`.
- Bootstrap replays `min(M_DISTRIBUTION_LOOKBACK + 1, len(hist))` rows. It uses the exact distribution
  predicate, assigns bar indices by `i - replay_row_count + 1` (`2 - replay_row_count` through `0`), and
  applies seeded thresholds only if the EMA-selected state is not correction. Live entries are allowed in
  `confirmed_uptrend` and `under_pressure`, and blocked only in `correction`; live distribution,
  correction-low, rally-undercut, and follow-through transitions are separately bound.
- All settings-backed distribution/follow-through thresholds, lookbacks, score weights, and bullish
  threshold are active-fixed optimizer candidates.

The RS/N/S/I inventory records:

- RS requires at least `10` ranked symbols. Standard history is
  `4 * TRADING_DAYS_PER_QUARTER`; the minimum fallback history is `60`, with
  `(1 + raw_return) ** (252 / observed_trading_days) - 1`.
- Technical evaluation requires `60` sessions and uses a `252`-session high window.
- N revenue score is `clip(revenue_growth / N_REVENUE_GROWTH_TARGET, 0, 2) / 2`, capped to `[0, 1]`.
  Proximity bands are `0.98`, `0.90`, and `0.75`; the lower-band factor is `0.3`.
- S power-gap inputs are default lookback `10`, gap `0.02`, and volume `1.5`. Minimum history is
  `lookback_days + 50`, but the executed half-open baseline slice is exactly
  `volumes.iloc[-(lookback_days + 50):-(lookback_days + 1)]`, containing `49` observations at the default.
  The policy also binds the exact
  50-session up/down-volume defaults, caps and score bands; float thresholds `50/200/500/1000`
  million with scores `1.0/0.85/0.65/0.4/0.2` and neutral `0.5`; and the volume/breakout `0.5/0.5`
  split with proximity floor `0.85`.
- I binds every ownership-level and ownership-trend threshold/formula, neutral unavailable score `0.5`,
  negative-trend floor `0.1`, and active-component reweighting.

Capacity/sizing and exits remain exact: default positions are uncapped, eviction is enabled, the sizing
formula is `portfolio_equity * position_risk_pct / stop_loss_pct`, risk is `0.01`, stop loss is `0.08`,
and scale tiers are `[[0.1, 0.25], [0.15, 0.25], [0.2, 0.25]]`. The early-winner flag from a `0.20`
gain within `15` held sessions suppresses tiered scale-outs only. Hard stop, stagnation, protective-stop,
and EMA exits remain active, and the flag clears at the start of processing when `days_held >= 40`.

## Built-in and injected attestation truth

Before each fresh capture, the owned built-in strategy is synchronized from the simulator for
`technical_only`, `require_bullish_market`, `require_proper_base`, and fundamental-provider mode. The
default provider marker is `legacy_scored_provider_path`; PIT uses
`pit_bundle_bound_provider_path`. Verification never synchronizes, so post-capture nested drift fails.
Provider objects are never serialized or accessed for data.

Built-in capture also requires `strategy is _owned_builtin_strategy`. The same identity relationship is a
digest-bound invariant leaf, without serializing object IDs. Replacing the strategy with another
`CanslimStrategy` of the same type rejects before a fresh capture; replacement after capture changes the
live leaf and fails verification. Injected mode is unaffected.

Injected strategies are not synchronized or introspected. Their Python type is advisory provenance only.
An optional JSON-safe `effective_policy_identity`, falling back to `checkpoint_identity`, is normalized and
digest-bound. Without one, policy scope is `engine_owned_envelope_only` and
`custom_internals_opaque_unattested=true`. With one, scope is
`engine_owned_envelope_plus_declared_custom_identity`. Two otherwise identical custom strategies declaring
versions `1` and `2` produced different digests:

- `3082b18be890bb4456c75c69b666328ef3af2a565e2f9d0d59094a1415255118`
- `901d76dc174c6e513faef87f6275ce75af86ca6240f3b3b80d703fcb7c87fae8`

Custom identity mutation after capture fails verification. Non-JSON-safe identities and raising identity
callables raise clear `ValueError`s. A minimal opaque custom strategy constructs without
`min_c_a_growth`.

The output contract is mode-specific: technical-only rebuilds completed-session technical facts but
bypasses C/A/RS/composite gates; full mode rebuilds technical facts and reapplies the canonical C/A/RS
non-M composite contract.

## Attestation lifecycle

- Constructor capture supports direct inspection.
- Official `run()` start synchronizes owned built-in fields and replaces the snapshot before cache clearing
  or data access, preserving supported pre-run simulator mutations.
- Verification freshly rebuilds the live object and digest, compares both to the stored object and digest,
  and independently hashes the stored object. It runs before every session's behavior, checkpoint
  fingerprint use, checkpoint/result construction, restored-result construction, and PIT publication.
- Live policy construction reads configuration and declared policy identity only. It does not read mutable
  portfolio/trade/price/cache/artifact state and does not trigger provider/data access.
- Canonical hashing remains sorted, compact UTF-8 JSON with `allow_nan=false`.

