## Self-review

1. Bootstrap now distinguishes constructor fallback, data-derived starting state, exact replay/indexing, and
   post-seed thresholds. S records the executed 49-observation slice rather than the explanatory 50-session
   comment. Both are active-fixed optimizer candidates.
2. Custom type provenance no longer implies configuration attestation. Declared identities are bound and
   live-verified; undeclared internals are explicitly opaque and scoped to the engine envelope.
3. Owned nested built-in state is synchronized only on capture and included in the policy. Built-in object
   identity is required on capture and independently live-attested, so same-type replacement cannot bypass
   the nested facts. Verification does not repair drift and therefore fails closed.
4. Existing run-start/session/checkpoint/result/publication verification and inert-request rejection remain
   intact. `core/engine_policy.py` has no runtime import from `core/backtest_engine.py`.
5. No active strategy threshold, formula, weighting, signal, entry, or exit behavior changed.

